Z||000000||maninblack||09-03-2000||06:35 AM||||can someone recommand me to look for some cool wheels for fiero,I have tried places<BR>like tire rack etc.nothing special there<BR>thx||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-03-2000||08:57 AM||||There have been as many threads about aftermarket wheels as there are aftermarket wheels.  Try doing a search using "wheels" as a topic.  You should come up with a weeks worth of reading.<P>That out of the way...What kind of wheels are you looking for?  I'm partial to the thick, 5 spoke ones.  MAS MGRs will probably fit my bill if I can get them in the correct offset (and they're fairly cheap, as wheels go).  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||maninblack||09-03-2000||04:28 PM||||thank you monkeyman,I"ll do just that.<BR>currently I have 16" 5 spoke which came with the car when I brought,somehow the offset is<BR>not right.It looks nice with the wheels sticking out abit but I wouldnt be able to have a full turn without rubbing the tires||||reg||14
Z||000003||Monkeyman||09-03-2000||04:36 PM||||What are they rubbing on?  The fenders?  With that kind of offset (making the wheels stick out) you should have no problem with a full turn.  Just the opposite.  Unless your wheels are just waaaay too wide to begin with.  What's the width?  Pics??||||reg||1
Z||000004||maninblack||09-04-2000||01:41 AM||||I dont realy knoe the offset but the rubber'<BR>is 255/50/16,only the left side rubs the inner plastic cover at the end of the full<BR>turn,as you said,i think those tires are too tall for fiero.by the way , how can I post<BR> the photo on this forum?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||09-04-2000||09:53 AM||||i have 255/50-16 on the back of mine but they don't stick out much. the wheel wells just look really full. they're on 16x7.5" panther 106's (3 stars). in front the same size wheel but with 225/50-16's. i think the offset is 35mm. i need to change to coilovers eventually. for now i just ground away a bit of the lower spring cup on my struts. can't recommend doing that though.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||09-04-2000||05:46 PM||||Just download PIP (Pennocks Image Poster) found in the blue box at the bottom of every page.  Follow the directions and you'll be posting pics in no time.||||reg||1
